{"name":"Afghan Hound","hex":"#e2d7b5","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Afghan Hound","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sighthound bred in Afghanistan to hunt hare and gazelle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Afghan_Hound"}],"entries":[{"title":"Afghan Hound","blocks":[{"text":"The Afghan Hound is a hound distinguished by its thick, fine, silky coat, and a tail with a ring curl at the end. The breed originates in the cold mountains of Afghanistan where it has been bred for speed and game hunting. Other names for this breed are Tāzī, Thasi, Barakzai Hound, and Balochi Hound."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Afghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Afghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afghan_Hound","wikidata":"Q21080"},{"title":"Hound","blocks":[{"text":"A hound is a type of hunting dog used by hunters to track or chase prey."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Beagle_GRUMPY2.JPG/330px-Beagle_GRUMPY2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hound","wikidata":"Q38923"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Afghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Afghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Afghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Afghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAfghan_dog_-_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Stamp_of_Afghanistan_-_1962_-_Colnect_647962_-_Afghan_Hound_Canis_lupus_familiaris.jpeg/500px-Stamp_of_Afghanistan_-_1962_-_Colnect_647962_-_Afghan_Hound_Canis_lupus_familiaris.jpeg?utm_source